# Installation

## CUDA Linux Laboratory

This project requires a CUDA-capable NVIDIA GPU and the CUDA toolkit with nvcc.

Check the environment with:

    nvcc --version
    nvidia-smi

Build and run:

    chmod +x run.sh
    ./run.sh

The script generates 200 test images, compiles the CUDA kernel, executes the GPU batch processing, and writes the 200 processed images to data/output/.
